<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 13 September, from 585 BCE to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-triumph.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">585 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,610 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tarquinius Priscus celebrates a triumph over the Sabines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-priscus">Lucius Tarquinius Priscus</a>, by Roman tradition the fifth king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, celebrated a triumph after defeating the Sabines, who ceded the town of Collatia in the peace that followed. The story belongs to the semi-legendary period before the Republic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-priscus">Tarquinius Priscus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph">Roman triumph</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">509 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Temple of Jupiter on the Capitoline Hill is dedicated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, the Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitoline Hill</a> was dedicated on the Ides of September in the Republic's first year, by the consul Marcus Horatius Pulvillus. Dionysius of Halicarnassus dated the consecration to 507 BCE.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitoline Hill</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">531 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Khosrow I becomes Sasanian King of Kings</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a>, known as Anushirvan, succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-i">Kavad I</a> as Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negus-nagast">King of Kings</a> and went on to negotiate an end to the Iberian War with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. He reigned until 579 and reformed taxation and the army.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-i">Kavad I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/533">533 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,493 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belisarius defeats the Vandal king Gelimer at Ad Decimum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the tenth milestone south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> defeated the Vandal army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a>, whose attempt to trap the invaders failed. Belisarius entered Carthage two days later, opening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>'s reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ad-decimum">Battle of Ad Decimum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">604 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,422 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sabinian is consecrated pope, succeeding Gregory the Great</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sabinian was consecrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, succeeding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i">Pope Gregory I</a>, who had died in March. A former apocrisiarius to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, he reigned during the Eastern Roman domination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> until his death in February 606.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i">Pope Gregory I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1759">1759 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">267 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wolfe defeats Montcalm on the Plains of Abraham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-wolfe">James Wolfe</a> climbed the cliffs above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> and defeated the French in a brief battle. Wolfe was killed and Montcalm mortally wounded; Quebec fell, sealing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The British bombard Fort McHenry in Baltimore</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British warships shelled Fort McHenry for some 25 hours. Seeing the flag still flying at dawn, Francis Scott Key wrote the poem that became 'The Star-Spangled Banner'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1993">1993 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">33 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rabin and Arafat shake hands on the Oslo Accords</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Israel and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine-liberation-organization">PLO</a> signed the Declaration of Principles at the White House, with a historic handshake between Yitzhak Rabin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasser-arafat">Yasser Arafat</a>. The deal created Palestinian self-rule, but lasting peace proved elusive.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1996">1996 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tupac Shakur dies after a drive-by shooting</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rapper Tupac Shakur died in Las Vegas aged 25, six days after being shot. One of hip-hop's best-selling and most influential artists, his murder long went unsolved.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 September <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-komnenos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-ii-komnenos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John II Komnenos</span><span class="tp">1087–1143</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cesare-borgia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cesare Borgia</span><span class="tp">1475–1507</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-reed"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-reed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Reed</span><span class="tp">1851–1902</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/constantin-caratheodory"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/constantin-caratheodory.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Constantin Carathéodory</span><span class="tp">1873–1950</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guntis-ulmanis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guntis-ulmanis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guntis Ulmanis</span><span class="tp">b. 1939</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
